      "title": "Public Address?",
      "desc": "Ask a STUN server",
      "detail": "Behind its home router the laptop knows only its private address, 192.168.1.10, which nobody on the internet can reach. So it asks a STUN server named in the call page’s settings, with one small UDP request. The answer says where the request seemed to come from, 198.51.100.7 port 61022: the router’s public address and the port its NAT opened for this conversation.",
