      "title": "Peer to Peer",
      "desc": "And when it can’t be",
      "detail": "The server helped the two browsers find each other, then stepped aside: the call goes straight between the two homes. When a network won’t let direct packets through (some company firewalls, some mobile networks), ICE falls back to a TURN server that relays the encrypted media without being able to read it. Group calls usually send media through a server too, called an SFU.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Media path",
          "Laptop to laptop"
        ],
        [
          "Fallback",
          "TURN relay (encrypted)"
        ],
        [
          "Group calls",
          "Usually via an SFU"
        ]
      ],
